            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pantry beetles live inside sealed-looking packages, spices, pet food and dried decorations, and the adults fly toward windows and lights, so you see them far from the source. Check every dry item including spices and pet treats. If the bugs are soft and pale rather than hard-shelled, they may be booklice responding to damp, not food."
