            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. Carpet beetle larvae, spider beetles and even booklice can turn up in bedding. Bed bugs are flat, oval, wingless and about the size of an apple seed, and they leave rusty spots and dark specks along mattress seams. Capture one on clear tape and compare it against the EPA description, or have your county extension office identify it."
          }
        }
