        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Small brown bugs in a house are rarely a mystery once you catch one and note where it was. Pantry beetles mean an infested package, so find it and seal everything else. Booklice, springtails and foreign grain beetles mean damp, so dry the room to about 50 percent and remove the cardboard and paper they live on. Carpet beetles mean natural fibers or pet hair, so vacuum and clean the food source out.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Bed bugs, fleas, ticks and cockroaches are the cases that justify a plan, a label-approved product or a professional. For everything else, cleaning, storage and humidity control will do more than any spray, and they keep working after the bottle would have run out.
          </p>
